<title>USA: Computer Task sets two-for-one stock split.</title>
<headline>Computer Task sets two-for-one stock split.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO, N.Y. 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer Task Group said on Tuesday its board approved a two-for-one common stock split effective June 2 to shareholders of record as of May 19.</p>
<p>The company said it thought a split would help CTG maintain an attractive market price range and was in the best interests of shareholders.</p>
<p>The company provides international technology services.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
